  "reason": "2026-09-30: the back fur hem (rest z 0.007-0.02 behind the heels, blender y > 0.18) sits on the floor. On the leg chain the stride plant's knee bend swung it under the stance floor (ground_glb refused the Move: planted LeftUpLeg sole lifted +0.091 at key 21, lowest other point RightLeg-owned); held on the Hips (the former bulwark_cloakhold rule) the 0.045 H stride pelvis drop took it under instead (+0.042/+0.057, Hips-owned); half-and-half still refused (+0.053/+0.064). Owned by the same-side foot, which the stride plant keeps on the floor, it passes. Numpy patch lane: tools/homm3_glb_patch, docs/homm3_glb_patch_lane.md. 2026-10-01 (CS bake v3 re-bake): the original ops (LeftUpLeg/LeftLeg and RightUpLeg/RightLeg -> same-side foot) tore more edges than the v3 export (the patch lane's stretch gate: 622 -> 640 edges past 2x over all 139 targets). The extra tears were on unchanged-weight edges at Blender z ~0.57-0.6 beside the right thigh, which the Corrective Smooth re-bake reached from the moved thigh share. Moving only the shin share (LeftLeg/RightLeg) plus the Hips split heals instead: 622 -> 560 edges, worst 6.965 unchanged. Measured in scratch on the v3 export: stride + cs_rekey + ground pass, and gate_faults is [] (as for the frozen delivery). 2026-10-11 (lane B authenticity): the DEF jotunn lifts the axe overhead and back at f1-f3 of AttackFront, brings it up in front at f4 and chops it level forward at f5-f6; the capture kept the axe hand low with the head pointing down. The axe arm is raised overhead f1-f3 and forward f4-f6, and the axe hand turned per key (keyRotations x2, split).",
